{"book":11,"chapter":10,"rubric":"MODERN FRONTEND / THE JAVASCRIPT LANGUAGE / CHAPTER 10","slides":[{"title":"The result comes later","sub":"Chapter 10 · Asynchrony","short":"Intro","main":"Callbacks, promises, async/await: three ways to describe \"later\".","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Operation runs","Result later","Three stages"],"captions":["A request goes to the server, the user clicks, a timer fires: no result right away","JavaScript is single-threaded: no stopping everything to wait; start an operation, the result comes later","Describing this \"later\" went through three stages: callbacks, promises and async/await"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"request →","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"…waiting…","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"code goes on","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":70.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"reply","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":130.0,"y1":56.0,"x2":224.0,"y2":56.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":130.0,"y1":100.0,"x2":224.0,"y2":100.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":290.0,"y":56.0,"text":"now","size":10.0},{"t":"text","id":"n2","x":290.0,"y":100.0,"text":"later","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s0","x":66.0,"y":70.0,"w":96.0,"h":34.0,"text":"callback","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s1","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":96.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Promise","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s2","x":294.0,"y":70.0,"w":96.0,"h":34.0,"text":"async/await","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e0","x1":114.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":124.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":228.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":238.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[14.6,25.8]}]},{"title":"Callbacks","sub":"Callback hell and trust","short":"Callbacks","main":"Callbacks lead to a staircase and scattered error handling.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Error-first","Callback hell","Trust"],"captions":["A function takes a callback and calls it when done; the error comes first, the result second","Three steps in a row nest inside each other: a staircase, with errors handled at every level","You hand control to someone else's function and hope your callback is called exactly once"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["fs.readFile(path, (err, data) => {","  if (err) return handle(err);","  use(data);","});"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":22.0,"lines":["a((e, x) => {","  b(x, (e, y) => {","    c(y, (e, z) => {","      done(z);","    });","  });","});"],"hl":[3],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":34.0,"text":"your callback","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"l","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":34.0,"text":"someone's function","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":150.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":208.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"0 times? twice? too early?","tone":"red","size":9.5}]],"cues":[11.3,23.4]}]},{"title":"Promise","sub":"States and subscription","short":"Promise","main":"A promise changes state only once.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Three states","Constructor","then and catch"],"captions":["A promise is the result of an unfinished operation: pending, fulfilled, rejected; one transition","The executor runs at once and gets resolve and reject; subscribers are always called asynchronously","Subscribe with then, and for errors with catch; a \"thenable\" is any object with then, promises unwrap it"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":90.0,"y":76.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"pending","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":270.0,"y":46.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"fulfilled","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":270.0,"y":108.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"rejected","tone":"red","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":140.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":220.0,"y2":52.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":140.0,"y1":82.0,"x2":220.0,"y2":104.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["const p = new Promise((resolve, reject) => {","  setTimeout(() => resolve(42), 100);","});"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["p.then((v) => console.log(v))","  .catch((e) => console.error(e));"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":300.0}]],"cues":[16.0,30.4]}]},{"title":"Chains","sub":"then, catch, finally","short":"Chains","main":"then returns a new promise: a flat list instead of a staircase.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Value","Promise","Error"],"captions":["then returns a new promise: a returned value becomes the result of the next link","If a handler returns another promise, the chain waits for it: a flat list of steps instead of a staircase","An exception rejects the next promise and travels down to catch; after catch you can go on, the error is \"recovered\"; finally doesn't change the result"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"s0","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"then → 1","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s1","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"then → 2","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s2","x":290.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"then → 3","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e0","x1":110.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":120.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":220.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":230.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["fetchUser(id)","  .then((u) => fetchPosts(u.id))","  .then((posts) => render(posts));"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["step1()","  .then(step2)      // throw → error goes down","  .then(step3)      // skipped","  .catch(recover)   // catches","  .then(next)       // we continue","  .finally(cleanup);"],"hl":[3,5],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[14.4,29.4]}]},{"title":"Order of execution","sub":"Microtasks","short":"Order","main":"Promise handlers run before timers.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Code","Queues","Result"],"captions":["First a timer with zero delay, then a promise with then, then a synchronous line","Promise handlers are microtasks: they run right after the current synchronous code, before timers","Output: \"sync\", \"promise\", \"timer\"; an endless chain of microtasks can freeze the page"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["setTimeout(() => log('timer'), 0);","Promise.resolve().then(() => log('promise'));","log('sync');"],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":24.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":80.0,"y":40.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"synchronous code","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":80.0,"y":80.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"microtasks","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":80.0,"y":120.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"timers","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":80.0,"y1":54.0,"x2":80.0,"y2":68.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":80.0,"y1":94.0,"x2":80.0,"y2":108.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":270.0,"y":80.0,"text":"everything from\nthe top queue\nfirst","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"o0","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"w":160.0,"h":26.0,"text":"1. sync","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"o1","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":160.0,"h":26.0,"text":"2. promise","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"o2","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"w":160.0,"h":26.0,"text":"3. timer","tone":"yellow","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.3,24.9]}]},{"title":"Combinators","sub":"all, allSettled, race, any","short":"Combinators","main":"Choose a combinator by what to do with an error.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["all","allSettled","race and any"],"captions":["Promise.all waits for all and returns results in the original order, but rejects on the first error","Promise.allSettled always waits for all and reports on each: fulfilled or rejected, and with what","race finishes with the fastest; any waits for the first success and rejects (AggregateError) only if all failed"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"p0","x":66.0,"y":40.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"A","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p1","x":66.0,"y":76.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"B","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p2","x":66.0,"y":112.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"C","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e0","x1":102.0,"y1":40.0,"x2":206.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":102.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":206.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":102.0,"y1":112.0,"x2":206.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":270.0,"y":76.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"[a, b, c]","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["await Promise.allSettled([ok, bad]);","// [{ status: 'fulfilled', value },","//  { status: 'rejected', reason }]"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":50.0,"w":140.0,"h":28.0,"text":"race: first (any)","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"w":140.0,"h":28.0,"text":"any: first success","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":290.0,"y":76.0,"text":"withResolvers:\npromise + resolve,\nreject","size":9.0}]],"cues":[16.8,29.3]}]},{"title":"async/await","sub":"Sugar over promises","short":"async/await","main":"An async function always returns a promise.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["async → promise","await","try / catch"],"captions":["A function marked async always returns a promise: a returned value is the result, an exception is a rejection","await pauses the function until the promise is ready, without blocking the rest of the program","Catch errors with plain try/catch; code reads top to bottom; top-level await is allowed in modules"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["async function f() {","  return 42;","}","f()   // Promise { 42 }"],"hl":[0,3],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["async function show() {","  const u = await fetchUser(1);   // pause","  const p = await fetchPosts(u.id);","  render(p);","}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["try {","  const data = await load();","} catch (e) {","  showError(e);","}"],"hl":[1,3],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}]],"cues":[12.3,29.5]}]},{"title":"Common mistakes","sub":"await, forEach, sequencing","short":"Mistakes","main":"Run independent work in parallel, not one after another.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Forgotten await","forEach","Sequentially"],"captions":["Forgotten await: you get a promise instead of a value, and its error goes uncaught","await inside forEach waits for nothing: use a for…of loop for sequential traversal","Two independent awaits in a row run one after the other: start both and wait with Promise.all"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["const user = loadUser(1);   // Promise!","console.log(user.name);   // undefined","","const ok = await loadUser(1);"],"hl":[3],"bad":[0,1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["items.forEach(async (x) => {","  await save(x);          // nobody waits","});","done();                   // too early","","for (const x of items) await save(x);"],"hl":[5],"bad":[1,3],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":19.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":80.0,"y":50.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"await a (1 s)","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":50.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"await b (1 s)","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t1","x":130.0,"y":76.0,"text":"2 s in a row","tone":"red","size":9.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":70.0,"y":110.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"a","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":70.0,"y":140.0,"w":80.0,"h":20.0,"text":"b","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t2","x":230.0,"y":120.0,"text":"Promise.all → 1 s","tone":"green","size":10.0}]],"cues":[9.1,32.9]}]},{"title":"Limiting concurrency","sub":"Pool and order","short":"Pool","main":"No more than the set number of tasks run at once.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Request avalanche","Worker pool","Result order"],"captions":["A thousand requests at once overload the server and exhaust the browser's connections","Several workers take tasks from a shared queue: no more than the set number run at once","Write results by index to keep the order; for search, take only the latest request into account"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"r0","x":50.0,"y":56.0,"w":44.0,"h":26.0,"text":"req","tone":"red","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r1","x":102.0,"y":56.0,"w":44.0,"h":26.0,"text":"req","tone":"red","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r2","x":154.0,"y":56.0,"w":44.0,"h":26.0,"text":"req","tone":"red","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r3","x":206.0,"y":56.0,"w":